qspacemidi (1.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship a monochrome tray icon and hand the desktop its name rather than a
    picture, so that KDE draws it from the icon theme and recolours it to the
    panel, the way the rest of the tray behaves.  The icon is installed as
    share/icons/hicolor/scalable/status/qspacemidi-symbolic.svg and follows
    the Breeze convention of painting with currentColor.
  * Keep the colourful icon where the desktop cannot look that name up - a
    build directory or the AppImage, whose files the panel process cannot
    see - because an icon it fails to find would leave a gap in the tray.
  * Add tray/iconStyle to choose: auto, monochrome or colour.

 -- Jakob Flierl <jakob.flierl@gmail.com>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:10:00 +0200

qspacemidi (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show the state a button is really in.  The driver assumed both buttons
    were released when it opened the device, so a button the receiver already
    held was inverted from then on: its press was swallowed as "no change"
    and its release lit the indicator.  Axes and buttons are now seeded from
    the device with EVIOCGKEY and EVIOCGABS at open.
  * Stop drawing an idle button indicator half lit: a row now knows whether
    it is a bipolar meter, which rests in the middle, or a lamp, which rests
    dark.
  * Keep a button indicator lit for at least 120 ms, so a tap that begins and
    ends within one frame is still visible.  The MIDI message is sent first
    and is never delayed by the indicator.
  * Follow the cap in the meters directly, at the rate the device reports,
    without the dead zone, the axis lock or the wait for the next CC update.
    The meters show what the device does; the rows below say what is sent.
  * Transmit the largest deflection seen since the previous CC update rather
    than the latest sample, so a quick flick of the cap is no longer lost to
    the update rate.
  * Only time out into the centre position on devices that report relative
    movement.  Absolute devices announce the centre themselves, and the
    kernel drops repeated equal values, so the timeout re-centred a cap that
    was merely being held still or moved slowly.  The timeout is configurable
    as input/idleTimeout.
  * Resynchronise with the device after SYN_DROPPED on Linux, where the
    kernel's event queue overflowed and events were genuinely lost.

 -- Jakob Flierl <jakob.flierl@gmail.com>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 14:45:00 +0200

qspacemidi (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Detect 3D mice again on Windows: the raw HID backend looked for a
    vendor-defined top-level collection, which no 3Dconnexion device
    actually exposes, so the mouse was never found.  Match the Generic
    Desktop / Multi-Axis Controller collection instead and verify that it
    declares the six axes.
  * Decode the input reports through HidP_* rather than fixed byte offsets,
    so both the wired SpaceNavigator, which splits translation and rotation
    over two reports, and the wireless models, which pack all six axes into
    one, are read correctly.
  * Take the axis range from the report descriptor on Windows instead of
    assuming +-512 and +-900, so full deflection reaches full scale.
  * Emit the axis signals from the Windows and macOS backends, without
    which the meters never moved and no MIDI was sent.
  * Show the product name of the device instead of its raw HID path.

 -- Jakob Flierl <jakob.flierl@gmail.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200

